-- The Interpretation Act (British Columbia), RSBC 1996, c. 238: the defined terms.
-- Pass 2. The catalogue holds every defined-term entry of ss 1, 8.1(1), 29, 29.1(1), 29.2 and 32(1) and the
-- cross-reference entries of s 29, in the order of the text. Each entry returns the meaning as the Act states it:
-- the words after the verb, what the entry names, what it leaves out, whether its list is closed, the conditions it
-- carries and the Acts it points at. A few definitions that a function can compute from facts follow the catalogue.
--
-- Draft. A single Sonnet 5.5 agent wrote this from the text alone; no domain expert has read it
-- against the statute. The quotations are copied from `RSBC-1996-c.-238.txt`, a plain-text
-- rendering made by a script (not the official text), by `srcrefs.py`; `src:N` is line N of that file.
--
-- The catalogue block (between the GENERATED markers) is written by `gen-terms.py` from `terms-data.py`:
-- the words, the quotation and the line numbers of every entry are copied from the text file by that script;
-- what each entry names, leaves out, points at and whether its list is closed is the encoder's reading, set down in
-- `terms-data.py` (NOTES.md, finding 8 says how it was checked, and what the check does not show).
--
-- "means" closes a list that it enumerates; "includes" does not. That is how the Act itself uses the two words
-- in s 29, and the membership rule below follows it (NOTES.md, fork F-open-list).
--
-- Target compiler: `unstable` (REFUSE and YMD are rejected by `main`).

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

§ `Types`

-- The Act says where each group of definitions applies; these are the lead-in lines. s 29 and s 29.2 say "In an
-- enactment" (their own lead-ins are quoted at the entries). The first two scopes apply everywhere the Act does.
-- src:9 | 1 In this Act, or in an enactment:
-- src:57 | 8.1 (1) In this section:
-- src:333 | 29.1 (1) Insofar as they can be applied, the following definitions apply in all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters:
-- src:363 | 32 (1) In this section:
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 1, s 8.1(1), s 29.1(1) and s 32(1) lead-ins (src:9, src:57, src:333, src:363)
DECLARE `Where a definition applies` IS ONE OF
    `In this Act, or in an enactment`
    `In an enactment`
    `In section 8.1`
    `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters`
    `In section 32`

DECLARE `How a term is defined` IS ONE OF
    `Means`
    `Includes`
    `Means and includes`
    `Is to be construed as`
    `Has the same meaning as in another enactment or agreement`
    `Has the prescribed meaning`
    `Refers to another entry`

DECLARE `Definition` HAS
    `the terms defined`        IS A LIST OF STRING
    `where it applies`         IS A `Where a definition applies`
    `how it defines`           IS A `How a term is defined`
    `the words of the Act`     IS A STRING
    `what it names`            IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it leaves out`       IS A LIST OF STRING
    `the list is closed`       IS A BOOLEAN
    `conditions it carries`    IS A LIST OF STRING
    `what it points at`        IS A LIST OF STRING

§ `The catalogue of defined terms`

-- Fields, in order:  the terms defined, where it applies, how it defines, the words of the Act (everything after the
-- verb), what it names, what it leaves out, the list is closed, conditions it carries, what it points at.
