-- src:10 | Act means an Act of the Legislature, whether referred to as a statute, code or by any other name, and, when referring to past legislation, includes an ordinance or proclamation made before 1871, that has the force of law;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 1 "Act" (src:10)
GIVETH A Definition
`s 1 definition of Act` MEANS
    Definition OF
        (LIST "Act"), `In this Act, or in an enactment`, `Means and includes`,
        "an Act of the Legislature, whether referred to as a statute, code or by any other name, and, when referring to past legislation, includes an ordinance or proclamation made before 1871, that has the force of law",
        (LIST "an Act of the Legislature", "an ordinance or proclamation made before 1871, that has the force of law"),
        EMPTY, FALSE,
        (LIST "when referring to past legislation"), EMPTY

