§ `How to ask the catalogue`

-- A scope that applies wherever the Act applies: s 1 and s 29 and s 29.2 say "in an enactment".
GIVEN scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a definition scope applies everywhere` scope MEANS
    CONSIDER scope
        WHEN `In this Act, or in an enactment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `In an enactment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `In section 8.1` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `In all enactments relating to treaty first nation matters` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `In section 32` THEN FALSE

-- Every definition of the term that applies in the scope the question is asked in. A definition made for a
-- section, a Part of the Act or a subject (s 8.1(1), s 29.1(1), s 32(1)) is preferred, in its own scope, to the
-- general one: "regulation" means one thing in s 1 and another "in this section" in s 8.1(1).
-- Cross-reference entries are not definitions, so they are left out.
GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A LIST OF Definition
`s 29 every definition of a term` term scope MEANS
    IF   `a definition scope applies everywhere` scope
    THEN general
    ELSE IF null specific THEN general ELSE specific
    WHERE
        named    MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD elem term (d's `the terms defined`) AND NOT (d's `how it defines` EQUALS `Refers to another entry`)) `all the entries of the catalogue`
        general  MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD `a definition scope applies everywhere` (d's `where it applies`)) named
        specific MEANS filter (GIVEN d YIELD d's `where it applies` EQUALS scope) named

GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE Definition
`s 29 the definition of a term` term scope MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 every definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN first FOLLOWED BY others THEN JUST first

GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE `How a term is defined`
`s 29 how a term is defined` term scope MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 the definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `how it defines`)

GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 29 the words the Act gives for a term` term scope MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 the definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING
        WHEN JUST d THEN JUST (d's `the words of the Act`)

GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 29 what the definition of a term points at` term scope MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 the definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
        WHEN JUST d THEN d's `what it points at`

GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
GIVETH A LIST OF STRING
`s 29 the conditions a definition of a term carries` term scope MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 the definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN NOTHING THEN EMPTY
        WHEN JUST d THEN d's `conditions it carries`

-- The cross-reference entries of the preamble of s 29: ["calendar year", see "year"].
GIVEN term IS A STRING
GIVETH A MAYBE STRING
`s 29 where a cross-reference sends the reader` term MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN d YIELD elem term (d's `the terms defined`) AND d's `how it defines` EQUALS `Refers to another entry`) `all the entries of the catalogue`
        WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
        WHEN first FOLLOWED BY others THEN
            CONSIDER first's `what it points at`
                WHEN EMPTY THEN NOTHING
                WHEN target FOLLOWED BY more THEN JUST target

§ `Named refusals`

@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29, s 1, s 8.1(1), s 29.1(1), s 29.2, s 32(1)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the Act defines no such term in that scope` MEANS
    REFUSE "the Interpretation Act defines no such term in that scope"

-- "includes" names some of the things a term covers and does not close the list; a "means" that describes the
-- meaning in words, with nothing listed, is not tested here against a thing. The refusal says which of these it is:
-- the first message is for "includes" and "means and includes", the second for "means", the third for the other
-- ways the Act defines a term (a rule of construction, the meaning in another enactment or agreement, a prescribed
-- meaning, a pointer to another entry).
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "includes" and "means"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definition does not list the thing` MEANS
    REFUSE "the definition does not list the thing: 'includes' leaves the list open, and a meaning given in words is not tested here against a thing"

@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "means"
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definition says what the word means in words and does not list the thing` MEANS
    REFUSE "the definition says what the word means in words and does not list the thing"

@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing` MEANS
    REFUSE "the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing"

-- Does the definition of a term name a thing? TRUE if the thing is named; FALSE if the definition leaves it
-- out, or if the list is closed and the thing is not on it; refused where the list is open and the thing is not on
-- it, or where the definition gives the meaning in words and lists nothing (three messages, by the verb). The words are matched as the Act writes them, so the question is asked in the Act's words.
GIVEN term  IS A STRING
      scope IS A `Where a definition applies`
      thing IS A STRING
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 the definition of a term names a thing` term scope thing MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 29 the definition of a term` term scope
        WHEN NOTHING THEN `the Act defines no such term in that scope`
        WHEN JUST d THEN
            BRANCH
                IF elem thing (d's `what it leaves out`) THEN FALSE
                IF elem thing (d's `what it names`) THEN TRUE
                IF d's `the list is closed` THEN FALSE
                OTHERWISE
                    CONSIDER d's `how it defines`
                        WHEN `Means` THEN `the definition says what the word means in words and does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Includes` THEN `the definition does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Means and includes` THEN `the definition does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Is to be construed as` THEN `the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Has the same meaning as in another enactment or agreement` THEN `the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Has the prescribed meaning` THEN `the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing`
                        WHEN `Refers to another entry` THEN `the definition gives the meaning in words or by pointing to another enactment, agreement or entry, and does not list the thing`

§ `Definitions a function can compute`

-- src:10 | Act means an Act of the Legislature, whether referred to as a statute, code or by any other name, and, when referring to past legislation, includes an ordinance or proclamation made before 1871, that has the force of law;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 1 "Act" (src:10)
GIVEN `it is an Act of the Legislature, by whatever name` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is an ordinance or proclamation`               IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day it was made`                              IS A DATE
      `it has the force of law`                          IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reference is to past legislation`             IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 1 an instrument is an Act` `it is an Act of the Legislature, by whatever name` `it is an ordinance or proclamation` `the day it was made` `it has the force of law` `the reference is to past legislation` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `it is an Act of the Legislature, by whatever name` THEN TRUE
        IF       `the reference is to past legislation`
             AND `it is an ordinance or proclamation`
             AND `the day it was made` BELOW YMD 1871 1 1
             AND `it has the force of law`
            THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

DECLARE `Holder of a corporation sole` IS ONE OF
    `Her Majesty`
    `The Lieutenant Governor`
    `Another holder`

DECLARE `Kind of body` IS ONE OF
    `An incorporated association`
    `A company`
    `A society`
    `A municipality`
    `Another incorporated body`
    `A corporation sole` HAS `whose` IS A `Holder of a corporation sole`
    `A body that is not incorporated`

-- src:232 | corporation means an incorporated association, company, society, municipality or other incorporated body, where and however incorporated, and includes a corporation sole other than Her Majesty or the Lieutenant Governor;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "corporation" (src:232)
GIVEN body IS A `Kind of body`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 a body is a corporation` body MEANS
    CONSIDER body
        WHEN `An incorporated association` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A company` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A society` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A municipality` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Another incorporated body` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A corporation sole` holder THEN
            CONSIDER holder
                WHEN `Her Majesty` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `The Lieutenant Governor` THEN FALSE
                WHEN `Another holder` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A body that is not incorporated` THEN FALSE

-- src:280 | newspaper, in a provision requiring publication in a newspaper, means a printed publication in sheet form, intended for general circulation, published regularly at intervals of not longer than a week, consisting in great part of news of current events of general interest;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "newspaper" (src:280)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 newspaper is defined only in a provision requiring publication in a newspaper` MEANS
    REFUSE "s 29 defines newspaper only in a provision requiring publication in a newspaper"

-- src:280 | newspaper, in a provision requiring publication in a newspaper, means a printed publication in sheet form, intended for general circulation, published regularly at intervals of not longer than a week, consisting in great part of news of current events of general interest;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "newspaper" (src:280)
GIVEN `the provision requires publication in a newspaper`          IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is a printed publication in sheet form`                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is intended for general circulation`                      IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is published regularly`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longest interval between issues, in days`                IS A NUMBER
      `it consists in great part of news of current events of general interest` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 a publication is a newspaper` `the provision requires publication in a newspaper` `it is a printed publication in sheet form` `it is intended for general circulation` `it is published regularly` `the longest interval between issues, in days` `it consists in great part of news of current events of general interest` MEANS
    IF   NOT `the provision requires publication in a newspaper`
    THEN `s 29 newspaper is defined only in a provision requiring publication in a newspaper`
    ELSE     `it is a printed publication in sheet form`
         AND `it is intended for general circulation`
         AND `it is published regularly`
         AND `the longest interval between issues, in days` AT MOST 7
         AND `it consists in great part of news of current events of general interest`

DECLARE `Land title legislation` IS ONE OF
    `The Land Registry Act`
    `The Land Title Act`

-- src:263 | land title legislation, prior to October 31, 1979 means the Land Registry Act and after October 30, 1979 means the Land Title Act;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "land title legislation" (src:263)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Land title legislation`
`s 29 the land title legislation on a day` day MEANS
    IF   day BELOW YMD 1979 10 31
    THEN `The Land Registry Act`
    ELSE `The Land Title Act`

-- src:321 | sureties means sufficient sureties, and security means sufficient security, and one person is sufficient for either unless otherwise expressly required;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "sureties" (src:321)
GIVEN `the number of persons expressly required, if the enactment requires one` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 29 the number of persons sufficient as sureties or as security` `the number of persons expressly required, if the enactment requires one` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the number of persons expressly required, if the enactment requires one`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN 1
        WHEN JUST required THEN required

DECLARE `Word of power or duty` IS ONE OF
    `May`
    `Must`
    `Shall`

DECLARE `How a word of power or duty is construed` IS ONE OF
    `Permissive and empowering`
    `Imperative`

-- src:270 | may is to be construed as permissive and empowering;
-- src:279 | must is to be construed as imperative;
-- src:319 | shall is to be construed as imperative;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "may", "must", "shall" (src:270, src:279, src:319)
GIVEN word IS A `Word of power or duty`
GIVETH A `How a word of power or duty is construed`
`s 29 how may, must and shall are construed` word MEANS
    CONSIDER word
        WHEN `May` THEN `Permissive and empowering`
        WHEN `Must` THEN `Imperative`
        WHEN `Shall` THEN `Imperative`

DECLARE `Where the word herein is used` IS ONE OF
    `In a section of an enactment`
    `In a part of an enactment`

DECLARE `What the word herein refers to` IS ONE OF
    `The whole enactment`

-- src:251 | herein used in a section or part of an enactment must be construed as referring to the whole enactment and not to that section or part only;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "herein" (src:251)
GIVEN used IS A `Where the word herein is used`
GIVETH A `What the word herein refers to`
`s 29 what the word herein refers to` used MEANS
    CONSIDER used
        WHEN `In a section of an enactment` THEN `The whole enactment`
        WHEN `In a part of an enactment` THEN `The whole enactment`

-- src:290 | prescribed means prescribed by regulation;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "prescribed" (src:290)
GIVEN `it is prescribed by regulation` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 a thing is prescribed` `it is prescribed by regulation` MEANS
    `it is prescribed by regulation`

-- src:310 | rural area means territory that is not in a municipality;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "rural area" (src:310)
GIVEN `the territory is in a municipality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 territory is a rural area` `the territory is in a municipality` MEANS
    NOT `the territory is in a municipality`

-- src:291 | proclamation means a proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor under the Great Seal issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 29 "proclamation" (src:291)
GIVEN `it is a proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor`        IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is under the Great Seal`                              IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 29 an instrument is a proclamation` `it is a proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor` `it is under the Great Seal` `it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council` MEANS
        `it is a proclamation of the Lieutenant Governor`
    AND `it is under the Great Seal`
    AND `it is issued under an order of the Lieutenant Governor in Council`

§ `s 32(1) Domestic and foreign enactments, and what counts as an amendment`

DECLARE `Jurisdiction of an enactment` IS ONE OF
    `British Columbia`
    `Canada`
    `Another province of Canada`
    `A jurisdiction outside Canada`

-- src:367 | domestic enactment means an Act or a regulation, or a portion of an Act or regulation, of British Columbia, Canada or another province of Canada;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 32(1) "domestic enactment" (src:367)
GIVEN place IS A `Jurisdiction of an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) an enactment is a domestic enactment` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
        WHEN `British Columbia` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Canada` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `Another province of Canada` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A jurisdiction outside Canada` THEN FALSE

-- src:368 | foreign enactment means an Act or a regulation, or a portion of an Act or regulation, of a jurisdiction outside Canada.
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 32(1) "foreign enactment" (src:368)
GIVEN place IS A `Jurisdiction of an enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) an enactment is a foreign enactment` place MEANS
    CONSIDER place
        WHEN `British Columbia` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `Canada` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `Another province of Canada` THEN FALSE
        WHEN `A jurisdiction outside Canada` THEN TRUE

DECLARE `A change to a domestic enactment` IS ONE OF
    `An amendment`
    `A repeal`
        HAS `it is replaced with a domestic enactment in relation to the same subject matter` IS A BOOLEAN
    `A revision`
    `A consolidation`

-- s 32(1) "amended ... includes (a) the repeal and replacement of the domestic enactment with a domestic
-- enactment in relation to the same subject matter, and (b) the revision or consolidation": a repeal that is not so
-- replaced is the case s 32(4) deals with separately ("repealed and not replaced"), so it is not an amendment.
-- src:364 | amended, in respect of a domestic enactment, includes
-- src:365 | (a) the repeal and replacement of the domestic enactment with a domestic enactment in relation to the same subject matter, and
-- src:366 | (b) the revision or consolidation of the domestic enactment;
@ref Interpretation Act (BC) s 32(1) "amended" (src:364-366)
GIVEN change IS A `A change to a domestic enactment`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 32(1) a change to a domestic enactment counts as an amendment` change MEANS
    CONSIDER change
        WHEN `An amendment` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A repeal` replaced THEN replaced
        WHEN `A revision` THEN TRUE
        WHEN `A consolidation` THEN TRUE

§ `The Schedule`

-- The Schedule describes "the line called the Cascade Mountains" (s 29 "Cascade Mountains"). It is a boundary
-- traced in legs ("thence ..."), from Boundary Point No. 7 to the southerly boundary of the Province. The legs
-- below are the text of the Schedule split at each "; thence ", by `gen-terms.py`; nothing here says where the line
-- runs on the ground, and no function asks whether a point lies on it.
